Say the headlines in the Gallup presidential
approval poll.

00:00:11.789 --> 00:00:12.789
Okay.

00:00:12.789 --> 00:00:17.789
So in the Gallup presidential approval poll,
Donald Trump is now polling 49% approval.

00:00:17.789 --> 00:00:22.660
This is as of Tuesday morning, which was before
the state of the union address a reality show

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:27.800
extravaganza that he did on Tuesday night
and before his acquittal on impeachment yesterday.

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:33.070
So we don't yet know how those two events
will affect his approval rating 50% according

00:00:33.070 --> 00:00:37.290
to the Gallup poll disapprove of Trump, 49%
approve.

00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:42.450
So a lot of Trump is have gone absolutely
crazy because of this and believe that Donald

00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:44.830
Trump is clearly a shoe in for reelection
in November.

00:00:44.830 --> 00:00:49.500
And of course they may be completely correct,
but what it is important to understand is

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:51.850
that this is just Gallop.

00:00:51.850 --> 00:00:59.020
It's much more uh, informative and contextualized
to look at an aggregate of Donald Trump's

00:00:59.020 --> 00:01:00.720
presidential approval.

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:07.620
And if you look at the aggregate both nationally
among all Americans or even among likely voters,

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:10.550
the approval rating has not moved very much
for Donald Trump.

00:01:10.550 --> 00:01:16.730
So let's look closely and as you can see from
the five 38 aggregate from approval rating,

00:01:16.730 --> 00:01:19.890
there really hasn't been, I would say not
much of an uptick.

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:21.330
There's really been no uptick.

00:01:21.330 --> 00:01:27.040
And Donald Trump's approval rating is actually
still on average lower right now than it was

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:28.110
in mid November.

00:01:28.110 --> 00:01:33.820
Now you can also counter by saying if Trump's
approval is historically low for a long period

00:01:33.820 --> 00:01:39.280
of time, when it becomes more normal, it looks
like a big increase.

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:42.880
But that actually ignores the data, which
is that Donald Trump's approval rating is

00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:44.299
basically steady.

00:01:44.299 --> 00:01:48.850
But the really important thing to think about
here is not actually whether Trump's real

00:01:48.850 --> 00:01:55.490
approval rating is at 49 47 or 42 the most
important message to take away from this is

00:01:55.490 --> 00:02:04.420
that regardless of whether it's at 49, 47
or 42, reelection remains likely for an incumbent

00:02:04.420 --> 00:02:08.300
president with an approval rating in the forties.

00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:14.150
The increase or decrease or the shift or the
exact number that's less important.

00:02:14.150 --> 00:02:20.830
What matters is that George W. Bush was reelected
in the year 2004 despite being relatively

00:02:20.830 --> 00:02:21.840
unpopular.

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:28.019
Now, there is no question that one can make
the case that it was because of irregularities

00:02:28.019 --> 00:02:31.310
only in the state of Ohio, which he won narrowly.

00:02:31.310 --> 00:02:35.939
And had he lost John Kerry would have become
president of the United States.

00:02:35.939 --> 00:02:41.159
But regardless, it came down to just a hundred
thousand votes in Ohio, even with, uh, Donald,

00:02:41.159 --> 00:02:46.939
uh, George W. Bush, not a particularly popular
president, uh, Barack Obama at this point

00:02:46.939 --> 00:02:52.939
in his presidency in the same Gallup presidential
approval poll, was it only 46% approval while

00:02:52.939 --> 00:02:54.849
Donald Trump again is at 49.

00:02:54.849 --> 00:03:00.510
So the important takeaways are it is really
difficult to knock out an incumbent president

00:03:00.510 --> 00:03:04.779
even with an approval rating in the forties
we've talked before about how you can make

00:03:04.779 --> 00:03:11.590
the mathematical case where a president could
actually be reelected even with an approval

00:03:11.590 --> 00:03:18.359
rating in the low thirties or the high twenties
now it would be unlikely because you need

00:03:18.359 --> 00:03:23.609
high support in certain States and then you
can mathematically have almost no support

00:03:23.609 --> 00:03:24.609
in certain state.

00:03:24.609 --> 00:03:26.269
Like you can do it because of the electoral
college.

00:03:26.269 --> 00:03:28.290
It's not the most likely scenario.

00:03:28.290 --> 00:03:35.090
But if it's possible to be reelected with
a 30% approval rating with a 49% of 47% or

00:03:35.090 --> 00:03:40.699
43% wherever it is you believe Donald Trump
actually is, it is no sweat to get yourself

00:03:40.699 --> 00:03:41.699
reelected.

00:03:41.699 --> 00:03:46.969
So this stuff really matters now in the next
week to two weeks.

00:03:46.969 --> 00:03:51.760
What I want to pay close attention to is what
happens to Donald Trump's approval in the,

00:03:51.760 --> 00:03:57.499
in the aggregate overall now that he has been
acquitted and impeachment and after that state

00:03:57.499 --> 00:04:01.029
of the union address and several very good
days in the stock market.

00:04:01.029 --> 00:04:05.659
And as we know, the stock market, something
that in practice affects way fewer people

00:04:05.659 --> 00:04:09.249
than it affects in ideology and for PR purposes.

00:04:09.249 --> 00:04:11.319
People see the stock market climbing.

00:04:11.319 --> 00:04:16.859
Even if they don't have shares of stock, they
